            <ArticleTitle>Intra-articular ganglia in the knee.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>322-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thirty-eight intra-articular ganglia were found in knees that were painful or had the symptoms of a mechanical derangement. During the period of study, 6,500 knees were examined arthroscopically by one surgeon. Thirty-five of the ganglia arose at the insertions of the cruciate ligaments. Excision of the ganglion yielded excellent results in 22 knees, good in 14, and fair in one.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
